# The atomic-server the data-browser talks to during local development.
#
# Only loaded by `vite dev` (mode=development) — production builds, which are
# served by atomic-server itself, have no such file and fall back to
# window.location.origin. This is the single knob for the "vite serves the SPA
# on a separate port from the server" dev edge case; there are no hardcoded
# vite ports anywhere in the app.
#
# Point this at the *managed node* (9885) rather than a standalone
# atomic-server (9883) when running the atomic-saas control plane locally.
# The control plane assigns every enrolled drive to that node, and the app
# reconciles its server URL to the enrollment's `http_origin` — so a drive
# created on 9883 gets silently repointed to 9885 mid-session, and everything
# (including resolving your own agent DID) fails if nothing is listening
# there. Creating drives directly on the managed node keeps the two in step.
VITE_ATOMIC_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:9885
